  "question": {
    "text": "For a transistor amplifier in common emitter configuration having load impedance of $1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega\\left(\\mathrm{h}_{\\mathrm{fe}}\\right.$ $=50$ and $h_{o e}=25$ ) the current gain is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-5.2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-15.7$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-24.8$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-48.78$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In CE configuration, $A_{\\mathrm{i}}=\\frac{-\\mathrm{h}_{\\mathrm{fe}}}{1+\\mathrm{h}_{0 \\mathrm{e}} R_{\\mathrm{L}}}$\n$=\\frac{-50}{1+25 \\times 10^{-6} \\times 1 \\times 10^3}=-48.78$"
  }
}